  "representation_invariants": [
    "A ManuallyDrop destination owns exactly source.len slots. Its registered length stays zero while shared spare-tail construction writes valid unpublished copies. Success publishes once and transfers ordinary Vec ownership.",
    "Production constructor failure performs no catch, observer, implicit Drop or deallocation. The allocation and completed prefix remain live exactly as native failed construction; insufficient-capacity assignment does not alter its receiver until the temporary copy succeeds.",
    "Test-only observation runs after element borrows have ended, asserts unpublished length zero, and captures fresh allocation provenance. A separate typed test owner destroys only the known completed prefix and releases the allocation after native state was asserted."
  ],
  "behavior_evidence": [
    "Fourteen C++ cases cover empty/retained-empty/single/retained sources, first/intermediate/final/long-final copy failures, empty/occupied insufficient-capacity assignment receivers, and first/intermediate/final temporary-copy failures. Thirty rows separate native states, live unpublished prefixes, and explicit test repair.",
    "The public Rust API executable invokes ordinary clone and assign with real native-style leaks and no recovery. All fourteen native state rows match exactly. The baseline library differs on five late failures through extra Rust-only Drop events and lower retained payload counts.",
    "The native fixture obtains its raw allocation pointer from actual placement-constructor this values, inspects only completed live elements, then explicitly destroys that prefix and calls Standard::Free. Capacity in unpublished rows is the constructor-requested source.Size; no failed C++ container object is read. Absent copied results use zero sentinel result fields.",
    "Strict Miri runs the shared construction path under cfg(test) observation and explicit typed allocation repair. It verifies every first/late failure allocation remains valid, prefix values/resources are observable before repair, and destruction/deallocation occurs exactly once. Public intentionally leaking failure probes are run normally, not falsely reported as leak-free Miri calls.",
    "Production rustdoc confirms construct_copy has only self and contains no copy_observed_into method. Test observation and catch/resume are absent from the production API/build. A dedicated unit test preserves identity of an owned panic payload through the test-only catch/resume.",
    "Successful public tests cover unallocated empty/retained-empty results, exact source-length capacity, independent owned payload identities, borrowed lifetimes/traits, zero-sized Rust safety, and sufficient-capacity assignment that must not invoke any copy constructor.",
    "Zero-sized failure tests safely recover the dangling aligned Vec representation with zero initialized values; usize::MAX capacity remains a Rust-only representation, not a native ABI claim.",
    "All forty-nine original test declarations join native/Rust and pass unchanged. Existing retained-assignment, Resize/SetValue/unpublished-tail, Insert/Erase/move/relocation tests remain green. No new allocator ownership hook or allocator/owned.rs change was introduced."
